.el .ds Aq '
.TH ckman-fido-access 1  ckman 
.SH NAME
ckman\-fido\-access \- Manage the FIDO2 PIN
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBckman\-fido\-access\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage the FIDO2 PIN
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
ckman\-fido\-access\-set\-pin(1)
Set the FIDO2 PIN (when none is set)
.TP
ckman\-fido\-access\-change\-pin(1)
Change the FIDO2 PIN
.TP
ckman\-fido\-access\-set\-min\-length(1)
Set the minimum PIN length (persistent authenticator configuration)
.TP
ckman\-fido\-access\-force\-change(1)
Force the user to change the PIN on next use
.TP
ckman\-fido\-access\-verify\-pin(1)
Verify the FIDO2 PIN against the CanoKey (resets the retry counter)
.TP
ckman\-fido\-access\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
